- Circulating fluidized-bed boiler; 

- Single Rotary Holding Furnace (RHF); 

- High temperature slag granulation system; 

- Oxygen plant. 

On installation of the copper ISASMELT™ plant, the intention was to shut down the FSR and reverberatory furnaces.  However, only one reverberatory furnace was shutdown in 1993, while the other reverberatory furnace and the FSR continued to operate until 1997.  Operation of the FSR and reverberatory furnace in parallel with the ISASMELT™ furnace resulted in constrained ISASMELT™ performance [2].  In order to increase the ISASMELT™ capacity to treat all of the Mount Isa concentrate and the concentrate from the new Ernest Henry mine, an upgrade was agreed in 1997. 

### **Upgrade 1** 

The changes to the installed equipment for the ISASMELT™ plant over the period 1997 to 2000 included [2]: 

- Replacing feed bins with a blending facility; 

- Installing a larger pelletizer; 

- Installing of a second 525 tonne per day (t/d) oxygen plant; 

- Upgrading the ISASMELT™ furnace off-gas Induced Draft (ID) fan; 

- Extending the length of the RHF; 

- Replacing the RHF slag granulation system with slag pot haulers; 

- Removing the air preheater. 

No design changes were made to the ISASMELT™ furnace itself. 

